abstract: >-
  An end-to-end 13-layer calibrated computational epigraphy benchmark across 5,679 Indus Valley
  inscriptions, featuring five-way known-answer and non-linguistic calibration (Ur III Sumerian,
  Linear B, Linear A, Non-Linguistic Stamps), exact 23-seal Max-CSP identifiability boundaries,
  Mohenjo-daro Copper Tablet internal Rosetta analysis, 700-year de-confounded paleographic drift
  chains, and a 690-inscription strict Leave-One-City-Out damaged restoration catalog.
